.Dd June 9, 2026
.Dt EFI 4D
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm efi
.Nd UEFI Runtime Services driver
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Pa /dev/efi
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver gives privileged user processes access to the UEFI variable
Runtime Services
.Pq GetVariable, GetNextVariableName and SetVariable
on systems booted from UEFI firmware.
It is the kernel component behind
.Xr efibootmgr 8 ,
which reaches it through the
.Sy libefivar
library.
.Pp
The driver attaches only on
.Sy i86pc
systems booted from 64-bit UEFI firmware, where the boot loader has
published the firmware's system table and memory map as the
.Sy efi-systab
and
.Sy efi-mmap
properties.
On a system booted through legacy BIOS, or one whose firmware is 32-bit,
the driver does not attach and
.Pa /dev/efi
is absent.
.Pp
All operations require the
.Sy PRIV_SYS_CONFIG
privilege.
Reading UEFI variables is privileged because some of them hold sensitive
data such as Secure Boot keys.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Pa
.It Pa /dev/efi
Character device providing access to UEFI Runtime Services.
.El
.Sh INTERFACE STABILITY
The
.Pa /dev/efi
ioctl interface is
.Sy Private .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr efibootmgr 8
.Rs
.%Q Unified EFI Forum
.%B Unified Extensible Firmware Interface (UEFI) Specification
.%U https://uefi.org/specifications
.Re
